Newvalues, a fictional duration parser written and reverse-engineered, does exactly that, and its logic here is straightforward to rephrase as code. A loose digit accumulator reads the character stream, and at each letter it records the collected digits as a numeric value. When it meets h it multiplies that value by sixty and adds it to a running total, and when it meets m it simply adds it on. Space characters are skipped, and the loop ends at the first character that is not a digit, a letter or a space.

