The grid uses only those two values, so I can rely on every cell to be either passable or a wall. An initial check confirms that the start and end cells are both 0. The rest of the function is a dynamic programming table where each cell records how many paths arrive at it: the top row and the leftmost column each hold a count of one, and any cell inside is the sum of the count in the cell above it and the count in the cell to its left. If any cell along the way is blocked, its count is zero and that keeps every downstream cell at zero as well, which matches asking the count from the first cell and stopping.

